WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:07.840
Can you tell me who the Chinese Bandits were and how that name came about?

2
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:16.060
Well, an exacting explanation can probably be gotten from Pete Finney [author of The Fighting Tigers 1893–1993], you know, in his book.

3
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.660
You know, but in essence,

4
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:29.680
I think it was born at the Alabama game when we were able to stop Alabama in the third and fourth quarter and hold on to win.

5
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:43.540
“Terry and the Pirates” was a famous comic strip in which [Paul] Dietzel liked to read and in there were descriptions of the most fierce warriors of the time:

6
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.220
the Chinese Bandits.

7
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:55.540
And he made the comment, you know, in post-game interviews that, “The third team played like Chinese Bandits.”

8
00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:00.480
And I think the press picked it up and started going with it and gave us that energy.
